KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* no copy: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* non-movable prvalue: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A functional cast `T(prvalue of T)' copies or moves instead of initializing
the object from the prvalue (N5008 [dcl.init.general]/16.6.1).  `T x =
f();' and `T x = T(4);' are fine.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program,
and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
